  [PASS] eta=0 limit reproduces solid-sphere Mori-Tanaka (vf=0.3): 5325.143 vs 5325.143 MPa

-- Premise checks ------------------------------------------------------------
  vf range 0-0.6 is below random close packing RCP=0.64 (monodisperse spheres): OK, but
  vf > ~0.55 in practice requires polydisperse packing; the vf=0.60 point is at the edge of
  what is realisable and real foams at that loading show particle-particle contact and damage.
  eta=0.9356 < 1 and true density 0.46 <= shell density 2.54: physically valid.
  Models are linear-elastic estimates; they do not capture particle crushing or matrix porosity.

